# Configuring NTP on a FortiGate (FortiOS 7.0.5)

On FortiOS 7.0.5 the NTP server setting is greyed out in the GUI, so it has to be set from the CLI. Newer versions don't need the `set interface-select-method specify` line, and you can set the interface straight away.

"10.0.0.17" is an example. Replace it with the IP of your NTP server (for example, a Windows Server with the NTP role), and set the interface to the FortiGate port that connects towards it.


config system ntp
    set ntpsync enable
    set type custom
    set syncinterval 60
    config ntpserver
        edit 1
            set server "10.0.0.17"
            set interface-select-method specify
            set interface "port1"
        next
    end
end
